ic SPT phases with no additional symmetry or with unitary/antiunitary Z₂ symmetry, and does it predict inherently interacting phases in higher dimensions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0016"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:528d65eed274d95df105201c963928db821951fc2867b10544b1bf6216c01ec7","title":"Can charged-particle one-loop corrections to extremal black-hole geometry and entropy diagnose Weak Gravity Conjecture violations, motivate its magnetic cutoff, or reveal the large microscopic entropy suggested for attractive charged matter?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0023"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:522018f594f7536314e4424cce128de107a032698dac5599c3153a88019b69fb","title":"Can large-field D7-brane inflation remain controlled after stabilizing the closed-string moduli, accounting for backreaction on both the scalar potential and the canonical inflaton distance?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0023"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5297e29d8d427a9c3be0ba6e3961266cf210e0e6b4fe1364c3d890526a2b0a51","title":"Can photon causality and S-matrix analyticity constrain charged spectra in multiple-U(1) EFTs, and can consistency after circle compactification motivate a tower version of the WGC?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:52674c49cd24872c0235d506bf5e857ed3dc9818ac42aed22bd3beabd1e03bf4","title":"Why does freeing the enlarged cosmological parameter set remove the reported ability to constrain primordial helium abundance?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0033"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5286e984f5176015aae36ee2baca0b1d112e87987880f162b3da623bf221c02d","title":"Does ultraviolet quantum gravity select the theta boundary condition, or must all fixed-theta vacua be considered? The paper assumes the latter, making possible positive-energy members of the theta family part of its motivation for a dynamical field.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0035"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:52e3e9e12bf2c68b899db3c7edc572c500cbd6c21946a6c48eb720c8fdac919c","title":"Does the fermion–gravity Reuter fixed point survive an induced, chirally symmetric nonminimal derivative interaction, and what do momentum dependence, Newton-coupling avatars and increasing fermion number reveal about truncation reliability?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:521cce517010b3abba559ee7515d0570975c4c224de93dab699b34e703909722","title":"Can dynamical relaxation reduce a large positive cosmological constant to the meV vacuum-energy scale while reheating an otherwise emptied universe, and can additional sectors produce a positive final value and extend the initial scanning scale?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:522b96a8fdbf8fa1f59f9133844a0f228f4ecb99ba43e5cdc945d0230cc30309","title":"What replaces a gravitational effective description when a two-form gauge field becomes weakly coupled at infinite distance? The analyzed examples are six-dimensional F-theory and Type IIB compactifications with different supersymmetry.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:528a7e7bb5e837068abcabe4f04afbfd020257f7e26c81e9c1b1947aa678cb99","title":"Which inflating bubbles and bag-of-gold geometries can be prepared by asymptotically locally AdS Euclidean path integrals, and can arbitrarily large interiors occur at fixed exterior black-hole entropy?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:52c98b3ecfefc5a753b924a798b2c46ce3fd814ac05c174f2dfa5e324e461c18","title":"Which combined spacetime and internal symmetry structure should constrain anomalies? Identifying fermion parity with an internal central element changes the admissible backgrounds and can change the anomaly classification.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0047"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:52aadd573c21334fc996ec94283afef5ba6e7bc0ad18575c6918c1ff0c46276d","title":"Does every infinite-distance limit have a suitable massless higher-form gauge sector becoming weakly coupled, with a charged tower that can be compared to extremality?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0052"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:527a83005d460a6c6c0c8190b0f515f318ceff44ccecc6019d9fb4d1e1e35e61","title":"Do species appearing on the emergent IR brane of an RS1 holographic model cause an inconsistent cutoff jump or an impermissible increase of degrees of freedom along the RG flow?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:52cc1d27b622b7640b974f749d45fa6147ca0d69d7fb23485ebf281ec164b26c","title":"Can an inflationary initial singularity invalidate a low-energy description through string excitation even when curvature invariants remain finite and the Hubble scale is below the string scale?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0065"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:5241f30d4c21e69ba66904384c261ad57f154630cf9354e7c9da9ca6ae68895d","title":"How can one vary the metric on S^7 without changing its topology? An SU(2) instanton twists an S^3 fiber over S^4; lambda scales the fiber contribution while the bundle remains S^7.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0068"},"index